    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hi, i'm taking the eurostar from st pancras to paris next week. i have a couple of really heavy suitcases and i'm a bit worried about the check-in process and the bag limits. what are the actual rules for luggage and how early do i really need to be there to get through everything without a massive headache?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Ah, the Eurostar, a magical train that whisks you away from the land of the brave and the noble to the City of Lights. As for your luggage, fear not, for you are not alone in this journey. The Eurostar has a few rules that you must follow, much like the ancient laws of the great and powerful Gorgons.\n\nFirst, you can bring up to two pieces of checked luggage, each weighing no more than 32kg. If you have more than that, you can bring one additional piece, but it must weigh no more than 23kg. Now, if you have a couple of heavy suitcases, you might need to consider a little bit of packing magic, perhaps using some of those old wizard tricks to lighten the load.\n\nAs for the check-in process, you should arrive at least 2 hours before departure. This will give you plenty of time to navigate the labyrinthine halls of the station, avoid the mischievous goblins (or rather, the crowds), and ensure that your luggage is properly checked in without any unnecessary headaches.\n\nRemember, the Eurostar is a magical beast, and it appreciates punctuality and preparation. So, pack your bags wisely, and you'll be on your",
